This product depends on @misofm/engine@0.1.0. The reviewed integration archive
was packed from misofm/engine commit
8a19a84813230713e8f1604db04be4dccf653283 with SHA256
5694c21f1e4eb99f6366d7bcc0330f0af06744768810edc3cc6e0e186df09488.
This records reviewed source/archive identity, not registry publication.

The incremental SHA-256 implementation and verified-store/session-gate
invariants were adapted from the issue-authorized misofm/engine stem-store
baseline at commit bd7f330a9773ce43bb077f0e6d5c8fc30fe9e27c.

The bounded PCM pump and its serialized Worker self-drive/control queue were
adapted from that same authorized Engine baseline. Ring allocation/writing,
scratch boot and the AudioWorklet feed now delegate to the Engine SDK. The
prior adapter copies of the MSB1 allocation/reader and feed mechanism came from
misofm/app commit 7485693e9bbcf2f65a91a4e5950e22d678d99062; their retained
attribution is shipped with the SDK that now owns these implementations.

This product includes libFLAC 1.5.0 from the Xiph.Org Foundation, built from
